  "scope": "Input to experiment E1. Each rule of the pinned catalog carries one class before any cohort is measured. A class change is a protocol amendment. Roles list where the rule's count enters a prevalence table; string roles stay in a separate layer. Revision 2 (September 11, 2026) admits the specification role beside documentation in every rule that admits documentation; the class of every rule is unchanged. Revision 3 extends the catalog with two advisory construction rules after review of development probes for #294. Existing classes and frozen measurements remain unchanged; no new association or editorial precision is asserted. Revision 4 adds four local editorial constructions developed on pinned Ptah excerpts. They are general style signals, not evidence of authorship or measured editorial precision. Revision 5 adds the unscoped-assurance construction from issue 299 as general style. Its development recall gain and lack of confirmation gain do not establish an authorship association; previous classes and frozen measurements remain unchanged. Revision 6 adds complete duplicate list items from issue 300 as general style. It preserves all previous classes and does not establish an authorship association or qualified defaults. Revision 7 adds adjacent word duplication, repeated claims and explanatory restarts as general style. No origin association or default qualification follows. Revision 8 adds instruction scaffolding and redundant predicates as general style. Previous classes stay unchanged; no origin association or default qualification follows.",
  "classes": {
    "general_style": "A general editing or readability rule kept whether or not it separates cohorts.",
    "explicit_prohibition": "A user-configured prohibition with no cohort hypothesis.",
